# A count that a loop reads whole, and steps: `sum += counter.count; counter.count--`. A load of a whole slot cannot take its value from a store to the low word of the slot: it waits until the store has
# reached the cache, so a turn costs several times what it should. Where a read of the whole slot runs about as often as the update, in its loop or behind it, the update stores the whole slot. A loop that only
# steps the count has no such read, and keeps the update of the low word.
